OL,3,GNEWSAGST will benefit Guernsey says
OL,4,AJersey tax expert
OL,5,
OL,6,FA Jersey tax consultant said Guernsey
OL,7,Fwould benefit from introducing a 3%
OL,8,Fgoods and services tax (GST) from 2029.
OL,10,FJohn Shenton, senior tax consultant at
OL,11,FGrant Thornton, said people in Guernsey
OL,12,Fwould "hate" the decision now, as
OL,13,FJersey people did ahead of its
OL,14,Fintroduction there in 2008, but "after
OL,15,Fa while you get used to it".
OL,17,FHe said he thought not exempting food
OL,18,Ffrom the tax had kept the overall rate
OL,19,Flower - and if the exemption had been
OL,20,Fbrought in the tax would now be closer
OL,21,Fto 10% instead of the 5% it had been
OL,22,Fsince 2011.
OL,23,APub: 06-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
